  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.35, pp. 271--272: the actual Steiner tube polynomial of every nonempty bounded convex S, every positive radius and all natural ambient dimensions; for open S in positive ambient dimension, genuine finite boundary rectifiability and actual Cauchy Hausdorff mass. Retain non-Borel and lower-dimensional sources, original normalized intrinsic volumes, degree-zero positive atoms and the two-atom line boundary.",
  "proof_route": "Independent Minkowski gauge and partial radial-map laws, proved local witnesses and the corrected inverse-gauge radial map give genuine boundary rectifiability. Actual convex line-fibre endpoints, projection multiplicity and 3.2.26 give Cauchy. Actual tube geometry, invariant projection composition, Fubini, the lower-dimensional induction, Gamma beta products, unit-ball Cauchy alpha normalization and scalar monomial integration give whole distance-level integrals. Apply 3.2.34 to closure distance and use independently proved original/closure volume agreement and additive splitting to restore the full-degree coefficient.",
